{
  "title": "cliff-cp: coverage failure of conformal prediction on activity cliffs (software and per-molecule records)",
  "upload_type": "software",
  "description": "<p>Analysis pipeline, fixed data splits, and per-molecule prediction records (70,170 test-molecule rows) accompanying the manuscript <em>\"How the coverage guarantee of conformal prediction fails on activity cliffs: mechanism, diagnosis, and a structural blind spot of applicability domains\"</em>.</p><p>Over 15 ChEMBL single-target datasets from the MoleculeACE benchmark, the repository reproduces: the cliff-versus-non-cliff coverage gap (18.2 percentage points at a nominal 90% coverage), an exact distribution-free <strong>coverage-transfer identity</strong> and the label-free diagnostic <code>net_mag</code> derived from it, the misalignment criterion that predicts which partition signals harm the cliff group, a decision-impact analysis quantifying how many true actives are discarded, and the structural blindness of applicability-domain filters to this failure mode.</p><p>All random seeds are fixed; every figure and table is regenerated by a documented command.</p>",
